{% comment %}
  The small drawing beside one name in a menu. The desktop mega menu's columns
  ('header-menu-drawer-links') and the mobile drawer's lists (sections/header_mobile) both carry
  it, so which file a name takes - and the fall back to a line icon when no picture ships for it
  - is decided once, here, and the two menus cannot drift apart.

  The pictures are files in Content > Files, named after the item's handle, one contract per set:

  - ring-styles  'ring-style-<handle>.png'   the ten engagement settings
  - band-styles  'band-style-<handle>.png'   the four wedding bands
  - shapes       'shape-outline-<handle>.png' the ten cuts, drawn face-on

  Replace a file in the admin and both menus take the new one up; the file name is the whole
  contract. A name taken off the list below - or one that never had a picture - falls back to the
  drawn icon in 'icon-ring-style', 'icon-band-style' or 'icon-diamond-shape' rather than leaving
  a broken image in the list.

  Accepts:
  - icons: {String} which set the list asks for: "shapes", "ring-styles", "band-styles",
      "types" or "stones". Anything else, including blank, draws nothing.
  - key: {String} the item's handle, e.g. "hidden-halo" or "oval". Handleize the item's own
      title, never its collection: "Round" is `round` under both Engagement and Diamonds, where
      the collections are 'round-engagement-rings' and 'round-diamonds'.
  - prefix: {String} the class the calling menu names its icon box with, e.g.
      "menu-drawer-desktop__link-icon". "--image", "--shape" and "--band" are appended to it, so
      each menu sizes the same markup for itself. Defaults to the desktop panel's.

  Only a list whose every name is drawn in the set it asks for may ask for it, or the names it
  misses each carry an empty box.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign icon_prefix = prefix | default: 'menu-drawer-desktop__link-icon'

  assign styles_with_images = 'solitaire,side-stone,halo,hidden-halo,three-stone,bridal-sets,vintage,nature-inspired,toi-et-moi,promise' | split: ','
  assign band_styles_with_images = 'wedding,anniversary,eternity,plain-metal' | split: ','
  assign shapes_with_images = 'round,oval,cushion,emerald,pear,princess,radiant,marquise,asscher,heart' | split: ','

  comment
    The box, not the file, is what holds a column level: the CSS fixes both sides and fits the
    picture inside, so these stay true whatever proportions a replacement file has. The width and
    height below are only the intrinsic hint that keeps the row from jumping before it loads.

    The cuts are square and sit in the same box the drawn icons take. The settings and the bands
    are wider than they are tall - each is drawn to 264px of ink on a canvas that follows its own
    height, so a band fills the width and the eternity ring, drawn face-on, fits by its height.
  endcomment
  assign icon_asset = ''
  assign icon_modifier = ''
  assign icon_width = 46
  assign icon_height = 32
  assign icon_source_width = 92

  if icons == 'shapes' and shapes_with_images contains key
    assign icon_asset = key | prepend: 'shape-outline-' | append: '.png'
    assign icon_modifier = ' ' | append: icon_prefix | append: '--image ' | append: icon_prefix | append: '--shape'
    assign icon_width = 28
    assign icon_height = 28
    assign icon_source_width = 56
  elsif icons == 'ring-styles' and styles_with_images contains key
    assign icon_asset = key | prepend: 'ring-style-' | append: '.png'
    assign icon_modifier = ' ' | append: icon_prefix | append: '--image'
  elsif icons == 'band-styles' and band_styles_with_images contains key
    assign icon_asset = key | prepend: 'band-style-' | append: '.png'
    assign icon_modifier = ' ' | append: icon_prefix | append: '--image ' | append: icon_prefix | append: '--band'
  endif

  comment
    The drawn icons are a `case` each with no `else`, so a name the set does not draw comes back
    an empty box rather than nothing at all. These are what each one covers; a name in neither
    its picture list nor this one carries no drawing, and the row closes up around the words.
  endcomment
  assign drawn = false
  case icons
    when 'shapes'
      assign drawn_keys = 'round,oval,cushion,emerald,princess,radiant,asscher,heart,marquise,pear,square,triangle,baguette' | split: ','
    when 'ring-styles'
      assign drawn_keys = 'solitaire,side-stone,halo,hidden-halo,three-stone,bridal-sets,vintage,nature-inspired,toi-et-moi,promise' | split: ','
    when 'band-styles'
      assign drawn_keys = 'wedding,anniversary,eternity,plain-metal' | split: ','
    when 'types'
      assign drawn_keys = 'studs,hoops-huggies,dangles-drops,climbers-jackets-cuffs,pendants,chains,charms,bracelets,rings,new-in,best-sellers' | split: ','
    when 'stones'
      assign drawn_keys = 'cubic-zirconia,lab-grown-diamond,pearl,shell-abalone,turquoise,black-onyx,opal,birthstone' | split: ','
    else
      assign drawn_keys = '' | split: ','
  endcase
  if drawn_keys contains key
    assign drawn = true
  endif
-%}

{%- if icon_asset != '' -%}
  <span class="{{ icon_prefix }}{{ icon_modifier }}" aria-hidden="true">
    <img
      src="{% render 'image-source', file: icon_asset, width: icon_source_width %}"
      alt=""
      width="{{ icon_width }}"
      height="{{ icon_height }}"
      loading="lazy"
    >
  </span>
{%- elsif drawn -%}
  {%- case icons -%}
    {%- when 'shapes' -%}
      <span class="{{ icon_prefix }}" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon-diamond-shape', shape: key -%}</span>
    {%- when 'ring-styles' -%}
      <span class="{{ icon_prefix }}" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon-ring-style', style: key -%}</span>
    {%- when 'band-styles' -%}
      <span class="{{ icon_prefix }}" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon-band-style', style: key -%}</span>
    {%- when 'types' -%}
      <span class="{{ icon_prefix }}" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon-jewellery-type', type: key -%}</span>
    {%- when 'stones' -%}
      <span class="{{ icon_prefix }}" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon-stone', stone: key -%}</span>
  {%- endcase -%}
{%- endif -%}
